ips between 1924 and 1928, so it was difficult to choose a favorite. The " [:a {:href "/results/28661"} "1924"] " gold medalist was Italy’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/56155"} "Giuseppe Tonani"] " and he was back in Amsterdam, but would finish only seventh. German " [:a {:href "/athletes/55868"} "Josef Straßberger"] " took a big lead with 122.5 kg in the press and held it after the snatch, leading by 10.0 kg over " [:a {:href "/athletes/55215"} "Rudolf Schilberg"] " of Austria. Schilberg dropped back to fifth, but Straßberger had an easy time winning the gold medal. Despite world records in the clean &amp; jerk by Estonian " [:a {:href "/athletes/55587"} "Arnold Luhaäär"] " and Czechoslovakia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/56798"} "Jaroslav Skobla"] ", Straßberger won by 12.5 kg, with Luhaäär second and Skobla third."] "\n\n" [:p {} "All three medalists would win further Olympic medals in weightlifting, with Skobla moving up to gold at " [:a {:href "/results/28814"} "Los Angeles"] ", while Straßberger dropped back to the bronze that year. Luhaäär again made the podium in " [:a {:href "/results/28884"} "Berlin"] " with a silver medal. Straßberger won the 1929 European title and then won a bronze medal at that event in 1930-31 and 1933-34, while Luhaäär finished second at the 1933 Europeans and won a bronze at the 1938 Worlds. Skobla had won the last World Championships held in this era, as a light-heavyweight, back in 1923. His son, " [:a {:href "/athletes/76699"} "Jiří Skobla"] ", won a " [:a {:href "/results/59427"} "shot put"] " bronze medal at the 1956 Olympics."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Kilograms"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/55868"} "Josef Straßberger"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-cent